# Your own data (PROJECT.md 4). It is never committed and so never pushed: `runBatch` takes the
# non-committing path when every write in a batch is under here, and git refuses `data` as a
# pathspec outright while this line stands. Removing it does not put the data back in history —
# it makes the app's commits fail instead. Provider requests can send chosen context; this rule protects personal files from Git pushes.
data/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
